    "Pass-2 cross-channel refinement improves per-channel accuracy (D:+11, K:+4, ESC:+12) but DEGRADES NN accuracy (105 to 85 full, 105 to 99 selective). Even selectively refining only improved channels creates INCOHERENT CRT tuples that don't correspond to valid characters. Oracle(P1,P2,Sel)=121 proves 16 complementary positions exist, but the information is inseparable from noise at the tuple level. MODULUS COMMENSURABILITY: small-modulus refinement helps (D from K, K from D, ESC from D) but large-modulus targets degrade (E from D: -20, b from D: -22). Per-channel accuracy is NECESSARY but NOT SUFFICIENT for NN improvement. All 7 channels must be refined CONSISTENTLY. Confirms the bloom coherence lesson from the opposite direction.", p101, 7);
