    "Z/9 collapse on the copy task requires BOTH a vulnerable seed AND sufficient depth. 4 seeds tested at SL=20: 3/4 show Z/9=88-91% (normal), 1/4 shows Z/9=10% (catastrophic, seed 14580). The pathological seed is normal at SL=5 (90%) and SL=10 (88%) but collapses at SL=20 (10%). Depth amplifies latent CD optimization pathologies: marginal-quality tables cascade at long sequence lengths. K-SPECIFIC mechanism: Z/8 (similar perturbation fraction, 12.5% vs 11%) is IMMUNE regardless of seed or depth. Z/49 (2% perturbation) universally robust. SOFTENS THM 272: Z/9 fragility is a stochastic vulnerability, not a universal depth effect. test_crt_lm_copy_transition.ax 13/13.",
    p273, 13);
  dom_append(dom_body(), s273);

  -- THM 274: POSITION-CAPACITY GATING (S2261)
  let s274 = make_section("700px") in
  render_h2(s274, "274. Position-Capacity Gating");
  render_p(s274, "Copy n-back: target = seq[n] for n=0..4 in 5-element sequence. PLUT shows STRONG position gradient, NOT invariance. Root cause: CD optimization has N/q samples per PLUT entry. Large channels (Z/49: ~10 samples/entry) overfit; small channels (Z/8: ~62) generalize. Position 0 is privileged by CD iteration order (identity default correct, never disturbed).");
  pf_result(s274, "PLUT n=0: 1400/1400 (100%). All channels perfect (THM 271 control).", "1400", 1);
  pf_result(s274, "PLUT n=1: 1213/1400 (87%). Z/49 drops to 13/200 (6.5%).", "1213", 1);
  pf_result(s274, "PLUT n=2: 858/1400 (61%). Z/25=7/200, Z/49=8/200.", "858", 1);
  pf_result(s274, "PLUT n=4: 472/1400 (34%). Most large channels fail.", "472", 1);
  pf_result(s274, "Z/8 and Z/11: 200/200 at ALL positions. Small channels immune.", "200", 1);
  pf_result(s274, "Z/49: 200 at n=0, 13 at n=1. Fails immediately at n>0.", "13", 1);
  pf_result(s274, "2D-LUT last-element (n=4): 714/1400 (51%). Identity-on-x is position-free.", "714", 1);
  pf_result(s274, "2D-LUT n=0 and n=2: 106-112 (chance). Memory barrier intact.", "106", 1);
  let p274 = 12 in
  pf_theorem(s274, "POSITION-CAPACITY GATING THEOREM",
    "PLUT copy accuracy decreases sharply with target position n (1400->1213->858->1022->472 at n=0..4). Small channels (Z/8, Z/11) are position-immune (100% at all n). Large channels (Z/49, Z/25) degrade because CD has too few samples per PLUT entry (N/q) to resolve the target position from noise. Position 0 is privileged: identity default is already correct, so CD never disturbs it. For n>0, CD must discover which position is the target -- this fails when samples per entry < ~20. 2D-LUT shows the complementary pattern: n=4 (last element) achieves 51% because identity-on-x is position-free learnable, while n=0/2 fail (memory barrier, THM 271). EXTENDS the capacity-gating framework: N/q per-entry sampling determines not just which channels learn, but which positions are accessible. test_crt_lm_copy_nback.ax 12/12.",
    p274, 12);
  dom_append(dom_body(), s274);

  -- THM 275: PATTERN EXTRACTION ASYMMETRY (S2262)
  let s275 = make_section("700px") in
  render_h2(s275, "275. Pattern Extraction Asymmetry");
  render_p(s275, "First abstraction task: extract common difference d from arithmetic sequence [v0, v0+d, v0+2d, v0+3d, v0+4d]. Target = d. Tests rule extraction (subtraction), not memory or accumulation. ARCHITECTURE INVERSION: 2D-LUT beats PLUT default -- opposite of copy task (THM 271).");
  pf_result(s275, "PLUT correct init (PLUT[0]=-x, PLUT[1]=x, PLUT[2-4]=0): 1400/1400 (100%).", "1400", 1);
  pf_result(s275, "2D-LUT additive default: 745/1400 (53.2%). State-dependence extracts d.", "745", 1);
  pf_result(s275, "PLUT default init: 538/1400 (38.4%). Additive ceiling limits CD.", "538", 1);
  pf_result(s275, "LUT shared: 299/1400 (21.4%). Arithmetic regularity partially extractable.", "299", 1);
  pf_result(s275, "Z/9 BEST in 2D-LUT: 154/200 (77%). K-channel dominates pattern extraction.", "154", 1);
  pf_result(s275, "Z/49: 21-45/200 (10-22%). Capacity-gated across all architectures.", "21", 1);
  pf_result(s275, "2D-LUT subtract init: 647/1400 (46.2%). Wrong basin (< additive 745).", "647", 1);
  let p275 = 9 in
  pf_theorem(s275, "PATTERN EXTRACTION ASYMMETRY THEOREM",
    "Task structure determines which architecture wins from default initialization + CD optimization. Copy task (THM 271): PLUT=100% >> 2D-LUT=chance because memory needs position-awareness. Pattern extraction (this theorem): 2D-LUT=53.2% > PLUT=38.4% because rule extraction needs state-dependent transitions. 2D-LUT exploits the arithmetic structure: after pos 0, h=v0 (identity on row 0). At pos 1, the (h=v0, x=v0+d) pair determines d. State-dependence extracts d from (h,x); additive PLUT cannot. PLUT correct init proves the architecture IS sufficient (100%) -- the gap is in optimization (CD from identity), not capacity. LUT at 21.4% (3x chance) shows arithmetic regularity is partially extractable even without position or state. All capacity-gated: Z/8=60-70%, Z/9=75-77% >> Z/49=10-22%. test_crt_lm_pattern.ax 9/9.",
    p275, 9);
  dom_append(dom_body(), s275);

